1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:01,480
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:06,580
I want to show an interesting effect, how the Tesla affects the current in the system.

3
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:11,780
We'll track the current through a current transformer on the inductor's hot end.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,500
Here it is, yellow channel load.

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,520
We have a 300W lamp.

6
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,600
This will be the consumption.

7
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:20,240
Turning on the push-pull.

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,940
Hear the characteristic sound.

9
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,680
Ok, consumption.

10
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,540
1.4A.

11
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:30,800
This is our current.

12
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,260
Now I'm turning on the Tesla.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,080
Interesting moment.

14
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,620
Feeding power to the Tesla converter.

15
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,120
Current jumped.

16
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,020
Adjusting synchronization a bit.

17
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:49,780
Influence visible.

18
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,500
Bringing hand close to the Tesla.

19
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,520
Missing starts in the pot core.

20
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,080
Influence going.

21
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,320
Here clearly visible the Tesla strike location.

22
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:07,380
No dead time.

23
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,760
Practically maximum current rise moment.

24
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,140
Turning off the Tesla.

25
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,560
No current in the circuit.

26
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,400
Starting again.

27
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:25,620
Can see how much current amplitude.

28
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:35,290
Practically, at minimum, a doubling occurs.

29
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:39,170
And that's it.

30
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:41,070
But this isn't the working mode.

31
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:43,470
Just tuned an interesting moment.

32
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:46,590
Consumption at the same level.

33
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:49,490
And here look what's happening with the lamp.

34
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:52,230
Now the Tesla isn't quite coordinated.

35
00:01:52,930 --> 00:01:54,510
It's suppressing current at output.

36
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,370
Turning it off.

37
00:01:58,330 --> 00:01:59,630
Bam, lamp lit up.

38
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:01,630
And consumption.

39
00:02:03,670 --> 00:02:04,730
And here I turn it on.

40
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:07,030
Bam.

41
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:10,430
Current in circuit grew.

42
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:12,570
Current at output decreased.

43
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:16,210
Moment worth attention.

44
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:19,170
We'll work a bit more.

45
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:22,450
And we'll need to tune the moment when the lamp will light up.

